{
  "source": "Prompts/unexpected-results-v5.mp4",
  "duration": 204.9493125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.48,
      "text": "Right now, you can find thousands of tech experts making incredibly confident, hyper-specific"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.48,
      "end": 9.52,
      "text": "predictions about exactly where artificial intelligence is heading."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.18,
      "end": 12.74,
      "text": "The best way to see it is a true story about rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.9,
      "end": 17.48,
      "text": "In 1902, the city of Hanoi was rapidly modernizing."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.18,
      "end": 21.86,
      "text": "The colonial government laid down miles of new state-of-the-art sewer pipes."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.84,
      "end": 27.72,
      "text": "Unfortunately, those dark, protected tunnels provided the perfect breeding ground for"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.72,
      "end": 29.38,
      "text": "a massive rat infestation."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.28,
      "end": 33.92,
      "text": "City officials devised what looked like a mathematically flawless solution."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.58,
      "end": 39.96,
      "text": "They created a bounty system, offering citizens a small cash payment for every severed rat"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.96,
      "end": 40.76,
      "text": "tail handed in."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.38,
      "end": 43.14,
      "text": "Initially, the metrics looked phenomenal."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.06,
      "end": 47.46,
      "text": "Tales poured into government offices by the thousands on a daily basis."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.12,
      "end": 52.86,
      "text": "But shortly after the program launched, citizens started noticing healthy, completely"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.86,
      "end": 55.46,
      "text": "tailless rats screwing around the city streets."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.06,
      "end": 58.24,
      "text": "The math had a biological loophole."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.02,
      "end": 61.72,
      "text": "A rat can survive perfectly fine without its tail."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.28,
      "end": 65.6,
      "text": "And more importantly, it can keep making more rat babies."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.4,
      "end": 70.36,
      "text": "The rat hunters figured out that killing the animal destroyed their own supply chain."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.02,
      "end": 75.82,
      "text": "So they caught the rats, clipped the tails to collect the cash, and released them back"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.82,
      "end": 77.06,
      "text": "into the sewers to breed."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.04,
      "end": 79.0,
      "text": "A dead rat pays once."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.96,
      "end": 81.84,
      "text": "A live rat pays forever."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.62,
      "end": 88.24,
      "text": "Some local entrepreneurs realized hunting wild rats was too much work, so they bypassed"
    },
    {
      "start": 88.24,
      "end": 91.48,
      "text": "the sewers entirely and set up dedicated rat breeding farms."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.52,
      "end": 96.44,
      "text": "The government eventually caught onto the scam and completely scrapped the bounty program."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.0,
      "end": 101.76,
      "text": "They were left with a literal mountain of severed tails in their offices, but the actual"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.76,
      "end": 106.7,
      "text": "living rat population in Hanoi was significantly higher than before the bounty started."
    },
    {
      "start": 107.42,
      "end": 112.52,
      "text": "But the real goal was fewer rats, and the program encouraged people to keep rats alive."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.28,
      "end": 114.86,
      "text": "Hanoi's plan was fewer rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.56,
      "end": 117.7,
      "text": "The unexpected result was more rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.34,
      "end": 119.68,
      "text": "Here are two more unexpected results."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.48,
      "end": 122.98,
      "text": "One welcome surprise, and one costly mistake."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.9,
      "end": 125.56,
      "text": "First, look at SMS text messaging."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.34,
      "end": 131.2,
      "text": "It was originally built strictly to send short, utilitarian messages over early mobile networks."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.9,
      "end": 134.62,
      "text": "Its creators did not expect it to be a primary feature."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.26,
      "end": 140.84,
      "text": "Instead, young users got hold of the technology and repurposed it, turning texting into a"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.84,
      "end": 143.32,
      "text": "daily, constant way to stay in touch with each other."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.74,
      "end": 146.92,
      "text": "Australia imported cane toads to eat beetles to storing sugar cane."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.5,
      "end": 151.68,
      "text": "They barely controlled the pests, poisoned native animals, and spread across the country."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.4,
      "end": 157.7,
      "text": "Now point that historical track record directly at the AI experts making today's headlines."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.24,
      "end": 161.98,
      "text": "Every AI expert working today is making a firm prediction about our future."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.56,
      "end": 167.44,
      "text": "These are smart, well-researched forecasts built on solid data from all camps."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.96,
      "end": 171.74,
      "text": "The most important thing AI does in your lifetime, good or bad,"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.16,
      "end": 176.88,
      "text": "may be something nobody in any camp, any lab, or any course has thought of yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.6,
      "end": 179.24,
      "text": "That's not a reason to fear the future."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.86,
      "end": 183.12,
      "text": "It's the reason to walk into it curious, with your eyes open."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.9,
      "end": 186.02,
      "text": "You do not need to predict the future perfectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.8,
      "end": 190.38,
      "text": "You need to recognize uncertainty, watch what people actually do,"
    },
    {
      "start": 190.38,
      "end": 193.82,
      "text": "and build skills that still matter when the forecast changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.62,
      "end": 199.68,
      "text": "As this final text banner highlights, some of the biggest results are the ones nobody predicted."
    },
    {
      "start": 200.6,
      "end": 202.38,
      "text": "That's the best reason to stay curious."
    }
  ],
